            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 87,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We can take out the todo, but I'd like to keep this tombstone code for when we routinely get asked why we don't enforce schemas at runtime.\n\nIdeally we'd make it a non-default meson option these days"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 87,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I do remember how in dbus-sensors everyone had their own little ```static bool debug = false;``` in the .cpp file to enable via patch file.\n\nThis piece of commented code has a similar smell.\n\nI can try to enable it via meson option, but do not want to test it since it will be default disabled and i see no good reason for anyone to enable it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 87,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> I do remember how in dbus-sensors everyone had their own little ```static bool debug = false;``` in the .cpp file to enable via patch file.\n\nThat log variables was a James thing;  Ideally what would be moved to at least one common debug variable, and std::format/printf.\n\n> \n> This piece of commented code has a similar smell.\n> \n> I can try to enable it via meson option, but do not want to test it since it will be default disabled and i see no good reason for anyone to enable it.\n\nThat's fine.  FWIW, There's VERY good reasons to enable it if you want to accept new configs on the fly securely, but doing that caused people that hadn't upstreamed their schemas to break, so.......  we do what's best for the greater industry.\n\nThat's fine if you don't want to test the enabled option, I just want something I can point people to when they scream about schemas not being enforced or EM crashing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 87,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@9elements.com",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "I think, we should enforce the validation as default and downstream people need to activly deactivate it via meson option or so.\n\nThe comment should refer the meson option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/configuration.cpp",
                    "line": 87,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I added a meson option for the runtime config validation.\n\nUntested, but at least now there is no patching required anymore to go via that code path."
                }
            ],
